## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple-idiomatic **`TelemetryGrid`** feature view at full parity with the web source `TelemetryGrid.tsx`, committed as `c6d524b78` (10 surface files + gate log, 1921 insertions).

**What was built** (following the established sibling `LiveTelemetryPanels` architecture):
- `TelemetryGrid.swift` (surface), `.State`, `.Adapter`, `.Model`, `.ViewModel`, `.Views`, `.Previews`, `.strings`, `.Tests`, `.ModelTests`
- Six tiles reproduced verbatim (Battery / Speed / Inside / Odometer / Charger / Sentry) with exact web tone thresholds, sub-labels, and SI→display unit conversion at the render boundary
- Binds through the shared P1/S8 `TelemetryGridSource` seam (no view I/O), uses `@/components/motion` parity (`TSStaggerContainer`/`TSStaggerItem`), emits the P1/S11 `view.opened`
- Every state renders: loading / data / empty / error + stale / offline (freshness chip, banner, one-shot stale auto-refresh)
- Zero English literals — all strings via the P1/S10 `TelemetryGrid` catalog; full VoiceOver/Dynamic Type/Reduce-Motion support

